WHAT THIS SOFTWARE ACTUALLY DOES
You are expected to understand this before you run it, because the code will not ask
twice:

  - It partitions, formats, and encrypts disks. Run against the wrong device, it
    destroys the existing contents of that device. That is generally not recoverable.
  - It writes LUKS headers and creates encrypted volumes. Losing a header or a
    passphrase loses the data behind it, permanently.
  - It is written to be run over OVHcloud's KVM/IPMI console against a bare-metal
    server, and it reboots that server as part of the install. A remote machine that
    fails to come back may require a support ticket, or physical hands, to recover.
  - It handles credentials, private keys, certificate material, and LUKS key files.
    You are responsible for the secrecy, permissions, storage, rotation, and
    destruction of every secret you put in its way.
  - It requests and renews TLS certificates and touches live web-serving state. A
    mistake can take an existing site offline or let a certificate lapse.
  - It can install packages and services, change SSH and firewall configuration, and
    alter boot and Secure Boot state, including clearing platform keys.

